# Wiring proof for the stdin= route: a bare `-` gets the PIPE.
#
# VALIDATES: the runner pipes a named stdin block into a command whose `-` is the
#   cliio stdin token, rather than writing the block to a file and substituting
#   the path (routeStdinBlock, internal/test/runner/runner_exec_util.go).
#   `ze-test peer` takes its expect script as a path argument and opens it
#   through cliio, so `-` reads standard input there.
# PREVENTS: the two shapes this branch had. The ze arm took the FIRST `-` in argv
#   whatever it meant, and the ze-peer arm appended a temporary file whether or
#   not the line carried a `-`, which left the `-` as argv[0] of the peer with
#   nothing on standard input: LoadExpectFile then read an EMPTY expect set and
#   the peer asserted nothing.
#
# Discrimination: the peer's own ASN comes from the piped block. A runner that
#   stops piping hands the peer no options at all, so it opens with the default
#   ASN, ze answers NOTIFICATION 2/2 Bad Peer AS and the session never
#   establishes. The expectation below can then never be met, whatever it says.

# ze-peer expectations, PIPED through the `-` on the cmd= line below.
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=asn:value=1
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=15s
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00300200000015400101004002004003040A0001FE400504000000C8180A0000
EOF_PEER

# One iBGP peer originating a single route from its own configuration.
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				next-hop 10.0.1.254
				local-preference 200
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 10.0.0.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT -:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=15s
